&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_9f11a9c769dfd22c-63&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;4,0&quot;&gt;As a Designated Support Engineer (DSE) at Asana, you’ll be the named technical support partner for a set of our enterprise customers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;4,2&quot;&gt;. You’ll build strong, ongoing relationships through personalized support, timely case management, and deep product expertise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;4,4&quot;&gt;. This is a hands-on role focused on delivering high quality, customer centric service to our most engaged users, ensuring that entitled customers receive responsive, thoughtful, and proactive support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;4,6&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_9f11a9c769dfd22c-64&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0&quot;&gt;In addition to owning support for your assigned accounts, you’ll also contribute to broader case queues, working cross-functionally with teams across Customer Support (including Technical Account Managers), Customer Success, and Product to help drive resolution and share insights&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2&quot;&gt;. You’ll thrive in this role if you’re detail oriented, collaborative, and passionate about helping customers succeed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
