&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pricing Strategy Director&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Monetization Strategy team drives Asana’s pricing/packaging strategy and execution, helping our customers get more value out of our offerings and capturing a fair share of that value.&amp;nbsp; We work cross functionally to deliver impactful offerings for team productivity and collaboration.&amp;nbsp; We’re helping to define the Work Management category and inventing new ways for teams to work more efficiently together and see the larger purpose behind their work.&amp;nbsp; Our team works directly with Product/Engineering, Sales/Support, Customer Research, Marketing, Data Science, Finance and Operations to deliver valuable offerings to our customers.&amp;nbsp; You’ll take part in every type of product work here – from strategy to product to process improvements – conceptualizing, launching, and iterating on Asana itself for millions of teams around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Pricing Strategy Director, you’ll play an instrumental role in building and executing Asana’s product monetization strategy. Reporting to the Head of Pricing and Packaging, you will partner closely with Product, Sales/GTM, Marketing, Finance and operational leaders to launch and optimize our monetization strategy to drive sustainable revenue growth and deliver an exceptional customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based in our San Francisco, New York, Chicago or Vancouver office with an office-centric hybrid schedule. The standard in-office days are Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday. Most Asanas have the option to work from home on Wednesdays. Working from home on Fridays depends on the type of work you do and the teams with which you partner. If you&#39;re interviewing for this role, your recruiter will share more about the in-office requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll achieve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With a focus on 1-2 business lines, drive the launch and optimization of our offerings: packaging, pricing model, price levels, and discount strategy.&amp;nbsp; Ensure it aligns with business objectives and strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an informed perspective on the business by examining operating metrics, customer data, and market trends to spot potential monetization opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to drive impact in short term (1Q) and long term (1-3 yrs), develop strategies to seize those opportunities, and drive decision making and organizational alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute detailed customer, product, competitor, and financial analyses to support the strategic recommendations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally (Product, Sales/CS, Finance, Operations) to create pricing and packaging recommendations, and confidently present these findings to the executive team (GMs, c-level, including CEO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate operational plan to implement monetization strategies, partnering closely with IT/Operations, Finance, Sales Enablement, and Deal Desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in determining pricing KPIs. Track, monitor, and report on the effectiveness of implemented pricing and packaging changes as well as health of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of pricing experience in strategy consulting / B2B software, which ideally includes 2+ years in pricing at enterprise-level SaaS companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in building pricing models, tools, and processes to optimize the pricing strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robust analytical skills, including customer/competitor research and financial analysis to help drive data-driven decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of SaaS pricing, self-serve (product-led) and sales-lead go-to-market strategies, and customer buying behaviors (SMB and enterprise customers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to cultivate impactful cross-functional relationships and lead diverse teams to achieve business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates curiosity about AI tools and emerging technologies, with a willingness to learn and leverage them to enhance productivity, collaboration, or decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with pricing and packaging research techniques (e.g., Conjoint, Van Westendorp) and proficiency in using survey tools such as Qualtrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with pricing trends in the marketplace, including AI pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Asana, we&#39;re committed to building teams that include a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, as this is critical to helping us achieve our mission. If you&#39;re interested in this role and don&#39;t meet every listed requirement, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’ll offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive compensation package plays a big part in how we recognize you for the impact you have on our path to achieving our mission. We believe that compensation should be reflective of the value you create relative to the market value of your role. To ensure pay is fair and not impacted by biases, we&#39;re committed to looking at market value which is why we check ourselves and conduct a yearly pay equity audit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For this role, the estimated base salary range is between $207,000 - $279,000. The actual base salary will vary based on various factors, including market and individual qualifications objectively assessed during the interview process. The listed range above is a guideline, and the base salary range for this role may be modified.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, your compensation package may include additional components such as equity, sales incentive pay (for most sales roles), and benefits. If you&#39;re interviewing for this role, speak with your Talent Acquisition Partner to learn more about the total compensation and benefits for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to provide equitable and competitive benefits packages that support our employees worldwide and include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health, wellness &amp;amp; fitness benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career coaching &amp;amp; support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term savings or retirement plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office culinary options to cater to your dietary preferences&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are just some of the benefits we offer, and benefits may vary based on role, country, and local regulations. If you&#39;re interviewing for this role, speak with your Talent Acquisition Partner to learn more about the total compensation and benefits for this role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Asana is a leading platform for human + AI collaboration. Millions of teams around the world rely on Asana to achieve their most important goals, faster. Asana has been named to Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces for 7+ years and recognized by Fast Company, Forbes, and Gartner for excellence in workplace culture and innovation. We offer an exceptional office-centric culture while adopting the best elements of hybrid models to ensure that every one of our global team members can work together effortlessly. With 13+ offices all over the world, we are always looking for individuals who care about building technology that drives positive change in the world and a culture where everyone feels that they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
